Falsifies `system_tests::user::tenth_pass_map_gate_tests::one_physical_page_is_never_writable_here_and_executable_there` (claim 11).

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect: the mapping hold's check compares each existing leaf of the frame with itself instead
of with the new mapping's flags. No single leaf is writable and executable, so the check never
fires, every path maps, and the tenth outsider pass's escape comes back: `MAP_RW` at one address
and `MAP_CODE` of the same frame at the next leave one page writable and executable in one space.
It is a one-word slip in the one line that names both sides of the pair.

Expected to fail: the assertion that `MAP_INTO` answers the code mapping with `NotPermitted`,
reporting `MAP_INTO mapped as code a frame the space maps writable at <writable va>`.

Replayed on 2026-10-31 (UTC) on aarch64 with `cargo xtask test --arch aarch64 --test
one_physical_page_is_never_writable_here_and_executable_there`: red at exactly that assertion,
writable at 0xffffffffe000.

diff --git a/kernel/src/revoke.rs b/kernel/src/revoke.rs
--- a/kernel/src/revoke.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/revoke.rs
@@ -447,7 +447,7 @@
                 }
                 if let Some((leaf_phys, leaf_flags)) = mmu::translate_at(root, e.va)
                     && leaf_phys == phys
-                    && leaf_flags.makes_writable_executable_pair(flags)
+                    && leaf_flags.makes_writable_executable_pair(leaf_flags)
                 {
                     return true;
                 }
